{
  "subtype": "what_if",
  "outcome_variable": "resolution_time",
  "per_column": [
    {
      "name": "ticket_category",
      "causal_role": "treatment",
      "named_in_query": true,
      "rationale": "The query is explicitly about reducing certain ticket types; ticket_category identifies the ticket type, the intervenable lever an actor could reduce/reroute."
    },
    {
      "name": "issue_mechanism_type",
      "causal_role": "confounder",
      "named_in_query": false,
      "rationale": "The underlying failure mechanism (connectivity, outage, access) affects both which ticket type is generated and how long resolution takes; not named in the query, and is a common cause rather than a mediator of the intervention."
    },
    {
      "name": "affected_resource_type",
      "causal_role": "confounder",
      "named_in_query": false,
      "rationale": "The affected resource shapes both the category of ticket and the intrinsic difficulty/resolution time; a plausible common cause not named in the query. However it is nearly collinear with ticket_category, weakening its independent confounding value."
    },
    {
      "name": "scope_breadth",
      "causal_role": "confounder",
      "named_in_query": false,
      "rationale": "Whether an issue is individual vs infrastructure-wide drives both ticket volume/type and resolution time; a common cause not named in the query."
    },
    {
      "name": "reassignment_indicator",
      "causal_role": "mediator",
      "named_in_query": false,
      "rationale": "Reassignment is a downstream consequence of the ticket type/workload that in turn lengthens resolution; it lies on the causal path and is a mediator, not a confounder."
    },
    {
      "name": "resolution_lag_bucket",
      "causal_role": "outcome",
      "named_in_query": false,
      "rationale": "This is a bucketed restatement of resolution_time, i.e., the outcome itself, not a confounder or treatment."
    }
  ],
  "treatment_present": true,
  "treatment_columns": ["ticket_category"],
  "treatment_intervenable": true,
  "confounders": [
    {"name": "issue_mechanism_type", "named_in_query": false, "plausibility": 0.7},
    {"name": "affected_resource_type", "named_in_query": false, "plausibility": 0.5},
    {"name": "scope_breadth", "named_in_query": false, "plausibility": 0.7}
  ],
  "confounder_quality": 0.6,
  "rationale": "The set correctly supplies an intervenable treatment (ticket_category / type), which an actor could reduce or reroute, matching the what-if framing. It adds several plausible confounders not named in the query (issue_mechanism_type, scope_breadth, and to a lesser degree affected_resource_type, which is largely collinear with category). However, the schema is diluted by a mediator (reassignment_indicator, on the causal path) and by resolution_lag_bucket, which merely re-encodes the outcome. Confounder coverage is moderate but real, so the interventional claim is partially satisfied."
}
```

